        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 扫兴",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "扫兴 — sǎoxìng — \"deflated; with the fun spoiled\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "下雨了真扫兴 xiàyǔ le zhēn sǎoxìng — It's raining. What a let-down."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 兴 (xìng) — six strokes in three pieces: at the top a dot, a second dot and a short stroke falling to the left; a long bar across; and under it 八 bā, two strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "扫兴 (sǎoxìng) is built from 扫 'to sweep' and 兴 (xìng) 'high spirits', both inherited from Middle Chinese, sawX and xingH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary glosses the first 'to sweep away'; it gives the second reading no gloss of its own, so 'high spirits' is the usual explanation, not a settled one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
